	 ('d2156abc-f6ad-40df-a9c0-326a2cd2022b'::uuid,'CRYSTALLINE STRUCTURE OF SOLIDS','SYSTEM','{"{\"название\": \"CRYSTALLINE STRUCTURE OF SOLIDS\", \"описание\": \"\\\"This entity refers to the arrangement and properties of crystals in solids. It is characterized by \"}"}','"This entity refers to the arrangement and properties of crystals in solids. It is characterized by a regular distribution of structural units (atoms, molecules, ions) within the solid and described through a crystal lattice." >','{}','{}','{"frequency": 1, "text_unit_ids": ["c443500ac401640e03812c68676ef2dc1b1766ba215011910bb4f476158764d339513dcb296b6be6ef5e21add844b582b4bb8f06949f4f8226ad3f8655aedb9b"]}','2026-07-17 17:14:05.801343','2026-07-17 17:14:05.801343','solid_state_physics_v1'),
	 ('47401964-c9ce-40a0-80d2-1bce24fa5410'::uuid,'CRYSTAL LATTICE','MODEL','{"{\"название\": \"CRYSTAL LATTICE\", \"описание\": \"The CRYSTAL LATTICE is a geometric model that represents the spatial arrangement of atoms, molecules\"}"}','The CRYSTAL LATTICE is a geometric model that represents the spatial arrangement of atoms, molecules, or ions within a crystal. This model is defined by three non-coplanar vectors known as lattice parameters, denoted as ''a'', ''b'', and ''c''. These vectors are crucial for understanding the periodicity and distribution of structural units (such as atoms, molecules, or ions) in space. Essentially, the CRYSTAL LATTICE provides a comprehensive description of how these fundamental units are organized and positioned within the solid structure of materials at atomic and molecular levels.','{}','{}','{"frequency": 2, "text_unit_ids": ["c443500ac401640e03812c68676ef2dc1b1766ba215011910bb4f476158764d339513dcb296b6be6ef5e21add844b582b4bb8f06949f4f8226ad3f8655aedb9b", "c443500ac401640e03812c68676ef2dc1b1766ba215011910bb4f476158764d339513dcb296b6be6ef5e21add844b582b4bb8f06949f4f8226ad3f8655aedb9b"]}','2026-07-17 17:14:05.801343','2026-07-17 17:14:05.801343','solid_state_physics_v1'),
	 ('adc922e2-b37d-45c5-8374-0918e48cad3a'::uuid,'LATTICE PARAMETERS (A, B, C)','MATERIAL','{"{\"название\": \"LATTICE PARAMETERS (A, B, C)\", \"описание\": \"Lattice parameters (A, B, C) are vectors that define the lengths and angles between them in the crys\"}"}','"Lattice parameters (A, B, C) are vectors that define the lengths and angles between them in the crystal lattice. These parameters are crucial for understanding the geometry and physical properties of crystalline structures. They play an essential role in determining key aspects of crystal morphology and material behavior."','{}','{}','{"frequency": 2, "text_unit_ids": ["c443500ac401640e03812c68676ef2dc1b1766ba215011910bb4f476158764d339513dcb296b6be6ef5e21add844b582b4bb8f06949f4f8226ad3f8655aedb9b", "c443500ac401640e03812c68676ef2dc1b1766ba215011910bb4f476158764d339513dcb296b6be6ef5e21add844b582b4bb8f06949f4f8226ad3f8655aedb9b"]}','2026-07-17 17:14:05.801343','2026-07-17 17:14:05.801343','solid_state_physics_v1'),
	 ('57f214a0-b198-4af9-bc07-7ebacfcc2d63'::uuid,'LATTICE PARAMETER','MECHANISM','{"{\"название\": \"LATTICE PARAMETER\", \"описание\": \"Three non-coplanar vectors (a, b, c) that define the positions in a lattice structure and help to re\"}"}','Three non-coplanar vectors (a, b, c) that define the positions in a lattice structure and help to reconstruct the spatial lattice completely>','{}','{}','{"frequency": 1, "text_unit_ids": ["be33f42641907295f83a337f4d06f95089e64774104fe7cec50db44a6a96d197ee77d4d46980237695981aeb6aed7f1827d31db11ce1ba5714986292f916aee0"]}','2026-07-17 17:14:05.801343','2026-07-17 17:14:05.801343','solid_state_physics_v1'),
	 ('95be3ce1-4aa8-41f2-8c70-a5ec595d2982'::uuid,'PRACTICAL APPLICATIONS OF SOLIDS','SYSTEM','{"{\"название\": \"PRACTICAL APPLICATIONS OF SOLIDS\", \"описание\": \"The practical applications of solids extend beyond their natural states and involve a deep understan\"}"}','The practical applications of solids extend beyond their natural states and involve a deep understanding of their crystalline structures. This knowledge is crucial for developing various technologies, including those used in space exploration and nuclear energy. The properties and structural analysis of these solids must be meticulously studied to effectively utilize them in everyday items and advanced technological applications. Thus, comprehending the intricate details of solid materials'' properties and structures paves the way for innovative practical uses across different fields, ensuring that we harness their full potential in real-world scenarios such as space missions and energy production processes.','{}','{}','{"frequency": 2, "text_unit_ids": ["c443500ac401640e03812c68676ef2dc1b1766ba215011910bb4f476158764d339513dcb296b6be6ef5e21add844b582b4bb8f06949f4f8226ad3f8655aedb9b", "c443500ac401640e03812c68676ef2dc1b1766ba215011910bb4f476158764d339513dcb296b6be6ef5e21add844b582b4bb8f06949f4f8226ad3f8655aedb9b"]}','2026-07-17 17:14:05.801343','2026-07-17 17:14:05.801343','solid_state_physics_v1'),
	 ('7e3bec8e-f0d1-4a77-b547-77e6c8daa6e0'::uuid,'TEACHING AID','MODEL','{"{\"название\": \"TEACHING AID\", \"описание\": \"TEACHING AID refers to a comprehensive educational document crafted to support both teachers and lea\"}"}','TEACHING AID refers to a comprehensive educational document crafted to support both teachers and learners in the study of physics. This resource encapsulates detailed explanations and discussions of fundamental physics laws and concepts, making it an essential tool for enhancing the understanding of these principles. It is designed to engage students through practical applications, offering solved problems that enable them to apply their knowledge effectively. Additionally, the document includes practice and self-assessment exercises, facilitating a deeper comprehension and reinforcement of learned material. Overall, TEACHING AID serves as a vital aid in ensuring both interactive and effective learning experiences within the realm of physics education.','{}','{}','{"frequency": 2, "text_unit_ids": ["c443500ac401640e03812c68676ef2dc1b1766ba215011910bb4f476158764d339513dcb296b6be6ef5e21add844b582b4bb8f06949f4f8226ad3f8655aedb9b", "c443500ac401640e03812c68676ef2dc1b1766ba215011910bb4f476158764d339513dcb296b6be6ef5e21add844b582b4bb8f06949f4f8226ad3f8655aedb9b"]}','2026-07-17 17:14:05.801343','2026-07-17 17:14:05.801343','solid_state_physics_v1');

