	 ('22ff0178-0b61-4c05-8b97-30f7acf3c46a'::uuid,'DU TEMPLE','PERSON','{"{\"название\": \"DU TEMPLE\", \"описание\": \"DU TEMPLE, an early aviation pioneer, played a significant role in the exploration of powered, contr\"}"}','"DU TEMPLE, an early aviation pioneer, played a significant role in the exploration of powered, controlled flight development alongside other notable figures. Du Temple constructed heavier-than-air manned machines capable of powered take-offs, reflecting advancements made during this critical period. Notably, Du Temple''s work encountered similarities with that of Sir George Cayley in terms of the fundamental challenges faced by pioneers in the field. Despite making important strides, Du Temple did not fully grasp the control concepts essential for successful and stable flight. This oversight was part of a broader set of issues that many early aviation enthusiasts grappled with as they endeavored to realize the dream of mechanized flight."','{}','{}','{"frequency": 3, "text_unit_ids": ["61646302e3bc960c352c6408cdc69191dab988abf38ec4bf7f2e4174aba91d86396e3e37ae38ca304afb1a34043af419361016661c11be52244507e7a8027a39", "61646302e3bc960c352c6408cdc69191dab988abf38ec4bf7f2e4174aba91d86396e3e37ae38ca304afb1a34043af419361016661c11be52244507e7a8027a39", "f5cd08a5bba8e5f1cac73b2168b03f440d049e82b880cf5ff9b03a61f932ab149f55ecbff1e2e45fc298cd176b96304c704c6f0d04ce87977c3be47e617c941b"]}','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','history_development_aeronautics'),
	 ('7a863021-c8ea-472e-80b9-36a9a1eedfb2'::uuid,'LIU BANG','PERSON','{"{\"название\": \"LIU BANG\", \"описание\": \"Liu Bang, a significant historical figure in China, is often associated with early innovations in av\"}"}','Liu Bang, a significant historical figure in China, is often associated with early innovations in aviation. According to available descriptions, Liu Bang reportedly invented the "wooden bird," which was likely a large-scale paper and wooden contraption designed for experimental flights around 400 AD. This invention reflects his contributions to the field of flight technology during antiquity. While there may be some uncertainty regarding whether Liu Bang actually invented the "wooden bird," these claims highlight his role as an innovator in early Chinese history. The date mentioned places this alleged invention within a period of significant cultural and technological development in China, suggesting that such attempts at mechanical birds for flight experiments were part of broader advancements during that era.','{}','{}','{"frequency": 2, "text_unit_ids": ["2e9ab909fa00e8633f612e2ff91a1104e10bcb90497c34e3402b71ef3457891e98b8a02caae3e6e229aac92c0c890dbd32b2f49dd7eb38da47a97c5e1a2a24ca", "93598286bf41252a5653b865693926a10004c8895f439d179e7df23951875f9be08961897007b5955c71dd93076ae3119f0c8ca810440b7e216291c012b3265d"]}','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','history_development_aeronautics');

