	 ('28bd577c-772d-4d7a-af48-cd71038acebf'::uuid,'MASS DENSITY','MATERIAL','{"{\"название\": \"MASS DENSITY\", \"описание\": \"MASS DENSITY is a fundamental property of matter that describes the amount of mass contained within \"}"}','MASS DENSITY is a fundamental property of matter that describes the amount of mass contained within a given unit volume. This physical quantity is typically calculated using the formula ρ = m / V, where ρ represents mass density, m is the mass, and V denotes the volume. In the International System of Units (SI), standard mass density for air at sea level (0 meters height) under International Standard Atmosphere (ISA) conditions is 1.225 kg/m³. The value can also vary based on other systems such as MKGSS (Metric Kilogram-Gravity-Sec制度), where the density of air at those specific standard conditions H=0m would be approximately 9.81 kg/m³. Notably, mass density is particularly relevant in defining properties of gases like air, where it aids in understanding their behavior under different conditions, often simplifying models by considering them as nearly incompressible fluids.','{}','{}','{"frequency": 3, "text_unit_ids": ["bf26f5a3b6530571e586bf2e521de1606936d166f7ecd17a2fda3301e6731802baf11ea7e937d0ec458325da1ec98c55af85370ad15325184313eb3e41a92807", "bf26f5a3b6530571e586bf2e521de1606936d166f7ecd17a2fda3301e6731802baf11ea7e937d0ec458325da1ec98c55af85370ad15325184313eb3e41a92807", "b5612dfd5afd1a966867270904e7977f694cbe6e96b4be34a53c32ab6f48a581ba2e0825a6d9165aaeb6957d598461f699ff9ff6c7b4ff82bb2c2e2dba4929d9"]}','2026-07-17 16:18:55.489892','2026-07-17 16:18:55.489892','aerodynamics_v1'),
	 ('991e7919-3e0a-4741-ba1e-abd38fa09724'::uuid,'CELSIUS SCALE','COMPONENT','{"{\"название\": \"CELSIUS SCALE\", \"описание\": \"One of the main scales for measuring temperature. It is defined based on the freezing and boiling po\"}"}','One of the main scales for measuring temperature. It is defined based on the freezing and boiling points of water at standard atmospheric pressure.','{}','{}','{"frequency": 1, "text_unit_ids": ["bf26f5a3b6530571e586bf2e521de1606936d166f7ecd17a2fda3301e6731802baf11ea7e937d0ec458325da1ec98c55af85370ad15325184313eb3e41a92807"]}','2026-07-17 16:18:55.489892','2026-07-17 16:18:55.489892','aerodynamics_v1'),
	 ('96342eed-f32c-4727-8105-ccc79b1c2810'::uuid,'STANDARD CONDITIONS (H=0M, ISA)','COMPONENT','{"{\"название\": \"STANDARD CONDITIONS (H=0M, ISA)\", \"описание\": \"(Defined set) Reference point for standard atmospheric conditions used in measurements and calculati\"}"}','(Defined set) Reference point for standard atmospheric conditions used in measurements and calculations of temperature, pressure, and density.','{}','{}','{"frequency": 1, "text_unit_ids": ["bf26f5a3b6530571e586bf2e521de1606936d166f7ecd17a2fda3301e6731802baf11ea7e937d0ec458325da1ec98c55af85370ad15325184313eb3e41a92807"]}','2026-07-17 16:18:55.489892','2026-07-17 16:18:55.489892','aerodynamics_v1'),
	 ('ff768147-5b9f-4510-ba54-85bc3fdeac38'::uuid,'AIR VISCOSITY','MATERIAL','{"{\"название\": \"AIR VISCOSITY\", \"описание\": \"Air''s viscosity changes with temperature; it increases as temperature decreases and is a key factor\"}"}','Air''s viscosity changes with temperature; it increases as temperature decreases and is a key factor in aerodynamics, influencing friction near streamlined bodies.','{}','{}','{"frequency": 3, "text_unit_ids": ["28cecdc770c6a89ca87abe00cc7c001435c36f85ccea49414b7b38e0ca90e9c7a34ae80b18f1142de6f051bd2874e60296f40c3fe63d476edda0f8036922ba4c", "28cecdc770c6a89ca87abe00cc7c001435c36f85ccea49414b7b38e0ca90e9c7a34ae80b18f1142de6f051bd2874e60296f40c3fe63d476edda0f8036922ba4c", "28cecdc770c6a89ca87abe00cc7c001435c36f85ccea49414b7b38e0ca90e9c7a34ae80b18f1142de6f051bd2874e60296f40c3fe63d476edda0f8036922ba4c"]}','2026-07-17 16:18:55.489892','2026-07-17 16:18:55.489892','aerodynamics_v1');

The streamtube is particularly useful for visualizing how changes in velocity at different points within a flow can affect pressure distribution according to Bernoulli’s principle. Despite the variability in cross-sectional areas, the conservation of mass and momentum holds true throughout the streamtube, ensuring that any increase o','{}','{}','{"frequency": 5, "text_unit_ids": ["ef6486c4db66ed7932b9bbcd3bcf3a0d6b5a54c10d03a87ac159ac59c84ab6e6992178768f4ec79d55ba89ac05ddc0f594857e23238ccbde9c113202d64a9956", "ef6486c4db66ed7932b9bbcd3bcf3a0d6b5a54c10d03a87ac159ac59c84ab6e6992178768f4ec79d55ba89ac05ddc0f594857e23238ccbde9c113202d64a9956", "b5612dfd5afd1a966867270904e7977f694cbe6e96b4be34a53c32ab6f48a581ba2e0825a6d9165aaeb6957d598461f699ff9ff6c7b4ff82bb2c2e2dba4929d9", "b5612dfd5afd1a966867270904e7977f694cbe6e96b4be34a53c32ab6f48a581ba2e0825a6d9165aaeb6957d598461f699ff9ff6c7b4ff82bb2c2e2dba4929d9", "2d9fdd18fbb30369988222506fc6af76775a9970c876b024d039f1156ef34f3f17266c64951a1221502b45b881305de03ffdda41d4d7de0a29ea5d1a8aa25ad3"]}','2026-07-17 16:18:55.489892','2026-07-17 16:18:55.489892','aerodynamics_v1'),
	 ('92e2e17b-adbd-4bcf-8354-1377eb736319'::uuid,'INCOMPRESSIBLE AIR','MATERIAL','{"{\"название\": \"INCOMPRESSIBLE AIR\", \"описание\": \"Assumption of constant density for air, useful in simplifying flow equations\"}"}','Assumption of constant density for air, useful in simplifying flow equations','{}','{}','{"frequency": 2, "text_unit_ids": ["b5612dfd5afd1a966867270904e7977f694cbe6e96b4be34a53c32ab6f48a581ba2e0825a6d9165aaeb6957d598461f699ff9ff6c7b4ff82bb2c2e2dba4929d9", "b5612dfd5afd1a966867270904e7977f694cbe6e96b4be34a53c32ab6f48a581ba2e0825a6d9165aaeb6957d598461f699ff9ff6c7b4ff82bb2c2e2dba4929d9"]}','2026-07-17 16:18:55.489892','2026-07-17 16:18:55.489892','aerodynamics_v1'),
	 ('f64d139e-fad0-497e-a8ea-95867904cbae'::uuid,'BERNOULLI''S EQUATION','MODEL','{"{\"название\": \"BERNOULLI''S EQUATION\", \"описание\": \"BERNOULLI''S EQUATION is a fundamental principle describing the behavior of fluids in steady flow co\"}"}','BERNOULLI''S EQUATION is a fundamental principle describing the behavior of fluids in steady flow conditions, specifically in low Mach number scenarios within a streamtube. This equation establishes the relationship between static pressure (\(P\)) and flow velocity (\(V\)), expressed as \( \Delta P + \frac{1}{2} \rho V^2 = \text{const.} \), where \(\rho\) is the fluid density. In simpler terms, it states that at any point in a streamline within such conditions, an increase in the kinetic energy (related to velocity) of a parcel of fluid results in a decrease in its static pressure.

For compressible flows, particularly relevant in scenarios involving gases with significant deviations from incompressibility, Bernoulli''s Equation can be extended to incorporate air temperature (\(T\)). The modified form, represented as \( \frac{k}{k-1} * R T + \frac{V^2}{2} = \text{const.} \), explicitly accounts for the temperature of the fluid and its effect on internal energy. Here, \(k\) is the specifi','{}','{}','{"frequency": 4, "text_unit_ids": ["b5612dfd5afd1a966867270904e7977f694cbe6e96b4be34a53c32ab6f48a581ba2e0825a6d9165aaeb6957d598461f699ff9ff6c7b4ff82bb2c2e2dba4929d9", "b5612dfd5afd1a966867270904e7977f694cbe6e96b4be34a53c32ab6f48a581ba2e0825a6d9165aaeb6957d598461f699ff9ff6c7b4ff82bb2c2e2dba4929d9", "2d9fdd18fbb30369988222506fc6af76775a9970c876b024d039f1156ef34f3f17266c64951a1221502b45b881305de03ffdda41d4d7de0a29ea5d1a8aa25ad3", "c8c5897c0dcab93d58d200fc9f0c15f81f8e093f6028b3f4e6d11e4efab906fb1aee05f08e53d8e44917ed87c14b9f1efbe47459b1d09dc02a6aff9bd1212cf2"]}','2026-07-17 16:18:55.489892','2026-07-17 16:18:55.489892','aerodynamics_v1'),
	 ('c3695204-f5d9-4c91-b935-2612c1030ce8'::uuid,'DYNAMIC PRESSURE','MECHANISM','{"{\"название\": \"DYNAMIC PRESSURE\", \"описание\": \"Dynamic pressure, also known as velocity head, is calculated by the formula q=(ρ V²)/2, kg/m², repre\"}"}','Dynamic pressure, also known as velocity head, is calculated by the formula q=(ρ V²)/2, kg/m², representing the kinetic energy aspect of the flow','{}','{}','{"frequency": 2, "text_unit_ids": ["2d9fdd18fbb30369988222506fc6af76775a9970c876b024d039f1156ef34f3f17266c64951a1221502b45b881305de03ffdda41d4d7de0a29ea5d1a8aa25ad3", "2d9fdd18fbb30369988222506fc6af76775a9970c876b024d039f1156ef34f3f17266c64951a1221502b45b881305de03ffdda41d4d7de0a29ea5d1a8aa25ad3"]}','2026-07-17 16:18:55.489892','2026-07-17 16:18:55.489892','aerodynamics_v1'),
	 ('9c738c5c-c182-473c-8925-aaa5a059cb22'::uuid,'TU-204 AIRCRAFT','DEVICE','{"{\"название\": \"TU-204 AIRCRAFT\", \"описание\": \"The Tu-204 aircraft is an aircraft that can fly at Mach numbers between 0.7–0.8, causing a temperatu\"}"}','The Tu-204 aircraft is an aircraft that can fly at Mach numbers between 0.7–0.8, causing a temperature increase of 28–37 °C at the leading edge of its wing and tail.','{}','{}','{"frequency": 1, "text_unit_ids": ["8a05132b3fe6468e796b195f5b301f4a392a4852762a881f2f6f451a4d3069e72d72d16a8d77bb430f4e65e71133a9dc1b87587f1ec920086287adb4a9ebcd43"]}','2026-07-17 16:18:55.489892','2026-07-17 16:18:55.489892','aerodynamics_v1'),
	 ('23244fec-db19-428e-b265-cd7bcc323de1'::uuid,'BODY SURFACE','COMPONENT','{"{\"название\": \"BODY SURFACE\", \"описание\": \"The surface of an object, here referring to the part of the aircraft wing or tail adjacent to the bo\"}"}','The surface of an object, here referring to the part of the aircraft wing or tail adjacent to the boundary layer','{}','{}','{"frequency": 1, "text_unit_ids": ["8a05132b3fe6468e796b195f5b301f4a392a4852762a881f2f6f451a4d3069e72d72d16a8d77bb430f4e65e71133a9dc1b87587f1ec920086287adb4a9ebcd43"]}','2026-07-17 16:18:55.489892','2026-07-17 16:18:55.489892','aerodynamics_v1'),
	 ('9b9fb4f6-f7af-407f-9537-3c119cd9916a'::uuid,'VISCOUS FRICTION FORCES','COMPONENT','{"{\"название\": \"VISCOUS FRICTION FORCES\", \"описание\": \"Forces that arise from air viscosity acting within the boundary layer and gradually reducing surface\"}"}','Forces that arise from air viscosity acting within the boundary layer and gradually reducing surface air velocity from zero to external speed.','{}','{}','{"frequency": 1, "text_unit_ids": ["8a05132b3fe6468e796b195f5b301f4a392a4852762a881f2f6f451a4d3069e72d72d16a8d77bb430f4e65e71133a9dc1b87587f1ec920086287adb4a9ebcd43"]}','2026-07-17 16:18:55.489892','2026-07-17 16:18:55.489892','aerodynamics_v1'),
	 ('c226481c-cc7f-4a79-9c11-e268580ef7cd'::uuid,'MAXIMUM SHEAR STRESS','COMPONENT','{"{\"название\": \"MAXIMUM SHEAR STRESS\", \"описание\": \"The entity \\\"MAXIMUM SHEAR STRESS\\\" refers to a critical concept in material mechanics. Maximum shear \"}"}','The entity "MAXIMUM SHEAR STRESS" refers to a critical concept in material mechanics. Maximum shear stresses occur on inclined sections within materials or structures and represent a significant mechanical property affecting structural integrity and material behavior under stress. Specifically, these maximum shear stresses are half the magnitude of the normal stress acting at those points. This relationship indicates that for any given point where normal stress is present, if there is an inclined section experiencing this stress, the maximum shear stress on that section will be precisely one-half of the normal stress value.','{}','{}','{"frequency": 2, "text_unit_ids": ["5854fa6da46c1055a30f7e997508937bc42323fe61136724756e5091e3379dbf8c367eccb6153126d536d89eb329b32ca7d3a54fd8d2249be567613ad490f3aa", "5854fa6da46c1055a30f7e997508937bc42323fe61136724756e5091e3379dbf8c367eccb6153126d536d89eb329b32ca7d3a54fd8d2249be567613ad490f3aa"]}','2026-07-17 16:45:38.667334','2026-07-17 16:45:38.667334','sopromat_v1');




