	 ('a08bb59f-b3e6-463f-a002-a8eb19557bd7'::uuid,'LILIENTHAL''S WHIRLING ARM','DEVICE','{"{\"название\": \"LILIENTHAL''S WHIRLING ARM\", \"описание\": \"(1891) \\\"An apparatus devised by Otto Lilienthal for testing wing forces and lift coefficients; it in\"}"}','(1891) "An apparatus devised by Otto Lilienthal for testing wing forces and lift coefficients; it involved rotating wings at high speed in open air, providing crucial data that advanced early aviation theory on aerodynamics."','{}','{}','{"frequency": 1, "text_unit_ids": ["4089000a7a5f43c1f79ebd955ed69dab8fc13c6f0153fe4c6ae9df3fdfa0ecdfc28e259193c210fc04e64e6f124fe76ccb1f7ccbb3e5ccb8e8d848fbdfd2ef5c"]}','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','history_development_aeronautics'),
	 ('db16155b-d35f-4a7b-9ef0-62094f423a37'::uuid,'ADER''S STEAM-POWERED MACHINE','SYSTEM','{"{\"название\": \"ADER''S STEAM-POWERED MACHINE\", \"описание\": \"The \\\"ADER''s Steam-Powered Machine\\\" was a pioneering steam-powered aircraft that demonstrated signif\"}"}','The "ADER''s Steam-Powered Machine" was a pioneering steam-powered aircraft that demonstrated significant advancements in early aviation technology. Developed by Louis-Dominique Ader, this machine marked the first successful steam-powered device capable of controlled flight, setting it apart from earlier attempts. Notably, on October 9, 1897, at Mont-Moulin La Gallette near Paris, Ader conducted a demonstration where the machine executed what appeared to be a "powered hop," marking an essential step in the development of aerial vehicles.
