	 ('52af2fcb-a35a-4cf4-ae9c-6de2f8de1cc6'::uuid,'3-METER DIAMETER WIND CHANNEL','SYSTEM','{"{\"название\": \"3-METER DIAMETER WIND CHANNEL\", \"описание\": \"The 3-meter diameter wind channel was first described in 1874 by French engineers Auguste de Louvrie\"}"}','The 3-meter diameter wind channel was first described in 1874 by French engineers Auguste de Louvrie and Jules Armagard. This simple device was designed for testing surfaces exposed to wind conditions within the three-meter diameter wind tunnel. Essentially, it comprised just a fan and a cylindrical tube, which together facilitated controlled airflow necessary for experimentation purposes. The primary function of this setup was to simulate various wind scenarios on test surfaces, thereby providing valuable data for researchers and engineers working in aerodynamics and related fields. This early design laid the foundational principles for modern wind channel testing techniques.','{}','{}','{"frequency": 3, "text_unit_ids": ["6cfb4419f8267d18f97a1bf9437f18c2fff2b46c4b4880ad7918290d562f0899526da9fb0c4b926965ffc8ef15460d197a1dd9b00d1923f6635f3ef8fdec8eaa", "6cfb4419f8267d18f97a1bf9437f18c2fff2b46c4b4880ad7918290d562f0899526da9fb0c4b926965ffc8ef15460d197a1dd9b00d1923f6635f3ef8fdec8eaa", "6cfb4419f8267d18f97a1bf9437f18c2fff2b46c4b4880ad7918290d562f0899526da9fb0c4b926965ffc8ef15460d197a1dd9b00d1923f6635f3ef8fdec8eaa"]}','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','history_development_aeronautics'),
