	 ('d79b2ca1-bf9f-4a4d-90d5-8193be34e9db'::uuid,'HANG GLIDERS','COMPONENT','{"{\"название\": \"HANG GLIDERS\", \"описание\": \"First glider design including flight control surfaces developed by Abbas ibn Firnas, flew for at lea\"}"}','First glider design including flight control surfaces developed by Abbas ibn Firnas, flew for at least ten minutes from Jabal al-''arus hill in 877 AD','{}','{}','{"frequency": 2, "text_unit_ids": ["ce6b5bf047905c10664374fb49d23d3216e192e2a564c6bafca1f58cbb43577b7a825598664c39e99d438a006e69f57882a5588711fddc205867ae05aa428ea2", "ce6b5bf047905c10664374fb49d23d3216e192e2a564c6bafca1f58cbb43577b7a825598664c39e99d438a006e69f57882a5588711fddc205867ae05aa428ea2"]}','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','history_development_aeronautics'),
	 ('8303032f-1acb-4daf-876f-e94d7397e5e9'::uuid,'KHARKIV NATIONAL AVIATION UNIVERSITY EXPERIMENTAL FACILITIES','SYSTEM','{"{\"название\": \"KHARKIV NATIONAL AVIATION UNIVERSITY EXPERIMENTAL FACILITIES\", \"описание\": \"Research institutions in Ukraine that have developed wind tunnel technologies as a fundamental compo\"}"}','Research institutions in Ukraine that have developed wind tunnel technologies as a fundamental component of their experimental aerodynamics programs.','{}','{}','{"frequency": 3, "text_unit_ids": ["c39119a42bf54d5f3a6c528527afa0659b9429b38912e2720b5ab4f6ac9e9979a2f0357e21700957de3eeda5bfae120fd0986c0cbb00355505e8e2ddc1e849ac", "c39119a42bf54d5f3a6c528527afa0659b9429b38912e2720b5ab4f6ac9e9979a2f0357e21700957de3eeda5bfae120fd0986c0cbb00355505e8e2ddc1e849ac", "c39119a42bf54d5f3a6c528527afa0659b9429b38912e2720b5ab4f6ac9e9979a2f0357e21700957de3eeda5bfae120fd0986c0cbb00355505e8e2ddc1e849ac"]}','2026-07-17 16:18:55.489892','2026-07-17 16:18:55.489892','aerodynamics_v1'),
	 ('f77a4257-e1c2-4f18-ae08-28e0614a7ea0'::uuid,'THERMAL FACTORS','COMPONENT','{"{\"название\": \"THERMAL FACTORS\", \"описание\": \"The entity \\\"THERMAL FACTORS\\\" encompasses critical aspects of fluid dynamics that play significant ro\"}"}','The entity "THERMAL FACTORS" encompasses critical aspects of fluid dynamics that play significant roles in the interaction between flowing fluids and solid bodies. These factors are especially vital in transonic and specialized aerodynamic studies, where temperature changes during flow interactions can significantly influence the performance and design optimization of aircraft and other aerospace technologies. Furthermore, thermal factors are also important in comprehensive flow-body interaction studies, emphasizing a thorough understanding of both mechanical and thermodynamic behaviors. This comprehensive analysis is crucial for ensuring reliable operation under various conditions and for advancing the field through more sophisticated modeling and testing methodologies.','{}','{}','{"frequency": 2, "text_unit_ids": ["c39119a42bf54d5f3a6c528527afa0659b9429b38912e2720b5ab4f6ac9e9979a2f0357e21700957de3eeda5bfae120fd0986c0cbb00355505e8e2ddc1e849ac", "c39119a42bf54d5f3a6c528527afa0659b9429b38912e2720b5ab4f6ac9e9979a2f0357e21700957de3eeda5bfae120fd0986c0cbb00355505e8e2ddc1e849ac"]}','2026-07-17 16:18:55.489892','2026-07-17 16:18:55.489892','aerodynamics_v1'),
	 ('33f8c634-40af-4878-adda-307628f4aa4b'::uuid,'TRYPILLIAN CERAMICS (WITH INDICATIONS OF SAILING)','MATERIAL','{"{\"название\": \"TRYPILLIAN CERAMICS (WITH INDICATIONS OF SAILING)\", \"описание\": \"Artifacts indicating the existence of early watercraft and the understanding of fluid dynamics by an\"}"}','Artifacts indicating the existence of early watercraft and the understanding of fluid dynamics by ancient civilizations.','{}','{}','{"frequency": 1, "text_unit_ids": ["c39119a42bf54d5f3a6c528527afa0659b9429b38912e2720b5ab4f6ac9e9979a2f0357e21700957de3eeda5bfae120fd0986c0cbb00355505e8e2ddc1e849ac"]}','2026-07-17 16:18:55.489892','2026-07-17 16:18:55.489892','aerodynamics_v1'),
	 ('39c5d4dd-e0ce-4779-8888-19dc1c8f2ad2'::uuid,'EILMER OF MALMESBURY''S FLYING MACHINE','DEVICE','{"{\"название\": \"EILMER OF MALMESBURY''S FLYING MACHINE\", \"описание\": \"Eilmer of Malmesbury''s flying machine, conceived around 1010 CE, represents a pioneering attempt in\"}"}','Eilmer of Malmesbury''s flying machine, conceived around 1010 CE, represents a pioneering attempt in aviation history. Although not successful due to limitations in available materials and knowledge of aerodynamics of the time, this prototype significantly influenced subsequent developments in flight technology. Eilmer’s visionary design served as an inspiration for later inventors, illustrating early human aspirations towards flight and contributing to the evolution of aviation theory and practice.','{}','{}','{"frequency": 2, "text_unit_ids": ["46b667214423448900a64449a21a8d78137e40dbbcde1ff7361b13892626a596937541e8a1dff8c28756c1af322bcfde1298239045005d93a04cd46043247c20", "46b667214423448900a64449a21a8d78137e40dbbcde1ff7361b13892626a596937541e8a1dff8c28756c1af322bcfde1298239045005d93a04cd46043247c20"]}','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','history_development_aeronautics'),
	 ('f6e9fa6d-9325-446a-90ff-f2169673b52b'::uuid,'MONTGOLFIER BROTHERS'' HOT-AIR BALLOON','DEVICE','{"{\"название\": \"MONTGOLFIER BROTHERS'' HOT-AIR BALLOON\", \"описание\": \"Developed by Joseph Montgolfier and Jacques-Etienne Montgolfier, first publicly demonstrated human f\"}"}','Developed by Joseph Montgolfier and Jacques-Etienne Montgolfier, first publicly demonstrated human flight in Paris 1783 using this hot-air balloon.>','{}','{}','{"frequency": 3, "text_unit_ids": ["624b0f2e5156161ffdb09c558f32b39ad0bf347e1dcc51d0cc803eb1592f75125b51005c9a82dfcfa9afb96df74b8311d90272937604af08308a19e41b14f3c5", "624b0f2e5156161ffdb09c558f32b39ad0bf347e1dcc51d0cc803eb1592f75125b51005c9a82dfcfa9afb96df74b8311d90272937604af08308a19e41b14f3c5", "624b0f2e5156161ffdb09c558f32b39ad0bf347e1dcc51d0cc803eb1592f75125b51005c9a82dfcfa9afb96df74b8311d90272937604af08308a19e41b14f3c5"]}','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','history_development_aeronautics'),
	 ('25db4826-fd95-44f3-a822-817c72dbda99'::uuid,'RUBBER-BAND MOTOR','MECHANISM','{"{\"название\": \"RUBBER-BAND MOTOR\", \"описание\": \"The RUBBER-BAND MOTOR is described as an alternative to both internal and external engines. This mot\"}"}','The RUBBER-BAND MOTOR is described as an alternative to both internal and external engines. This motor serves as a simpler and more controlled solution, offering an easier-to-manipulate method for generating mechanical energy compared to conventional engines, which may be powered by various means including chemical reactions like those involving gunpowder. The rubber-band motor thus provides a practical substitute that is likely less complex, potentially safer, and more straightforward to operate in educational or experimental settings where precision control is required.','{}','{}','{"frequency": 2, "text_unit_ids": ["faa334cc3a5b50c3cebcf1df46beb7be9ad777690802933a651dec6cbd0da34c9fef6dd95627eca4b6a746fc7c67bc72b217d1c4e60e92895dbfef4b8412f573", "faa334cc3a5b50c3cebcf1df46beb7be9ad777690802933a651dec6cbd0da34c9fef6dd95627eca4b6a746fc7c67bc72b217d1c4e60e92895dbfef4b8412f573"]}','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','history_development_aeronautics'),
	 ('ebd049f5-b471-4fae-be26-7f88265d54d5'::uuid,'ASPECT RATIO','MECHANISM','{"{\"название\": \"ASPECT RATIO\", \"описание\": \"The term \\\"Aspect Ratio\\\" is a characteristic that describes the relationship between the length and w\"}"}','The term "Aspect Ratio" is a characteristic that describes the relationship between the length and width of wings. This metric is crucial for comparing different wing designs with the aim of enhancing lift performance. The aspect ratio is often utilized in various aerodynamic studies, including Wenham''s wind tunnel tests, to assess and optimize flying objects such as airplanes, unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs), or other aircraft models. By analyzing this parameter, engineers can make informed decisions about wing design to improve efficiency and effectiveness in terms of lift generation while also considering factors like drag and structural integrity.','{}','{}','{"frequency": 2, "text_unit_ids": ["a1689fa4557c7bd9828498b6af22e4d56a6e70b706bc03a66df0ec58854f6cb93cfb6e67be14e6cf7954609e79e3b6bd423a0ba59422819f13f132672854041e", "a1689fa4557c7bd9828498b6af22e4d56a6e70b706bc03a66df0ec58854f6cb93cfb6e67be14e6cf7954609e79e3b6bd423a0ba59422819f13f132672854041e"]}','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','history_development_aeronautics'),
	 ('aa212d95-4ea7-413a-878d-27e681dde3be'::uuid,'ROYAL AERONAUTICAL SOCIETY OF GREAT BRITAIN','ORGANIZATION','{}','The Royal Aeronautical Society of Great Britain was established in 1866. This society played a pivotal role in advancing aerial and mechanical flight through academic research and presentations. Notably, John Joseph Waterston Wenham, an esteemed engineer, made significant contributions at this nascent stage by presenting his groundbreaking research on various engineering devices within the organization. These studies were instrumental in laying foundational principles that eventually led to the development of wind tunnels—a critical tool for aerodynamic testing. Consequently, the Society of Great Britain''s early support and Wenham''s pivotal presentations have solidified its legacy as a cornerstone institution in the field of aeronautics, contributing significantly to advancements in aviation technology over the subsequent decades.','{}','{}','{"frequency": 2, "text_unit_ids": ["a1689fa4557c7bd9828498b6af22e4d56a6e70b706bc03a66df0ec58854f6cb93cfb6e67be14e6cf7954609e79e3b6bd423a0ba59422819f13f132672854041e", "a1689fa4557c7bd9828498b6af22e4d56a6e70b706bc03a66df0ec58854f6cb93cfb6e67be14e6cf7954609e79e3b6bd423a0ba59422819f13f132672854041e"]}','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','history_development_aeronautics'),
	 ('bba824f4-7682-4090-be14-2f6dab123661'::uuid,'KYIV NATIONAL AVIATION UNIVERSITY WIND TUNNEL FACILITY','COMPONENT','{"{\"название\": \"KYIV NATIONAL AVIATION UNIVERSITY WIND TUNNEL FACILITY\", \"описание\": \"Component at Kyiv National Aviation University used to conduct similar types of experiments\"}"}','Component at Kyiv National Aviation University used to conduct similar types of experiments','{}','{}','{"frequency": 1, "text_unit_ids": ["4d79766d7c102666e5cbdcf972aa2ca84c504f89f7c9e735d66b3b9901f21bb74741741169d93c5909e55918a8ed41113434da52d7537b0cef2a603e49c9dc6e"]}','2026-07-17 16:18:55.489892','2026-07-17 16:18:55.489892','aerodynamics_v1');
