	 ('d9462338-f641-4f5b-aede-1a78987c9d49'::uuid,'NEWTON''S IMPACT THEORY OF AERODINAMIC DRAG','MECHANISM','{"{\"название\": \"NEWTON''S IMPACT THEORY OF AERODINAMIC DRAG\", \"описание\": \"This theory proposed in the 17th century dominated science until the 20th century and served as a fo\"}"}','This theory proposed in the 17th century dominated science until the 20th century and served as a foundation for modern rarefied gas aerodynamics','{}','{}','{"frequency": 2, "text_unit_ids": ["179038fe517a80b11687045f8990ed7f43f61ddac3ac215566be7a632476947416100235bd283fbe165b968ddf404e87c54967e59bf89b7b6d8260c5e4cb485f", "179038fe517a80b11687045f8990ed7f43f61ddac3ac215566be7a632476947416100235bd283fbe165b968ddf404e87c54967e59bf89b7b6d8260c5e4cb485f"]}','2026-07-17 16:18:55.489892','2026-07-17 16:18:55.489892','aerodynamics_v1'),
	 ('5be904c0-5d8c-43ba-86e7-d0ca14b8f355'::uuid,'CRYSTAL GEOMETRY','MODEL','{"{\"название\": \"CRYSTAL GEOMETRY\", \"описание\": \"The entity \\\"Crystal Geometry\\\" is characterized by the distinctive geometric formations that arise fr\"}"}','The entity "Crystal Geometry" is characterized by the distinctive geometric formations that arise from diffraction patterns. These formations are a direct result of the periodicity and symmetry evident in the arrangement of atoms within crystal structures. Diffraction patterns, which occur when waves (such as X-rays or electrons) pass through a crystal, reveal the underlying atomic lattice''s orderly arrangement with remarkable precision. This systematic structuring leads to the predictable and often aesthetically pleasing shapes observed in crystalline materials, making them a subject of both scientific study and artistic admiration.','{}','{}','{"frequency": 2, "text_unit_ids": ["00143051310245f816588fb716da03e26c16bc4e7bceee44f164ad9fcb43cb30be624db6179e62ee993abaffba0e87685e16d6a70ad71f73a8df1bbb25b96d33", "00143051310245f816588fb716da03e26c16bc4e7bceee44f164ad9fcb43cb30be624db6179e62ee993abaffba0e87685e16d6a70ad71f73a8df1bbb25b96d33"]}','2026-07-17 17:14:05.801343','2026-07-17 17:14:05.801343','solid_state_physics_v1'),
