	 ('c950308b-f418-44d5-9504-3d9814a19adf'::uuid,'BOW SHOCK WAVE','PART','{"{\"название\": \"BOW SHOCK WAVE\", \"описание\": \"A bow shock wave is a type of shock wave ahead of a blunt body where deceleration and compression oc\"}"}','A bow shock wave is a type of shock wave ahead of a blunt body where deceleration and compression occur abruptly; it can form during supersonic flow around revolution bodies or wings','{}','{}','{"frequency": 2, "text_unit_ids": ["140849ef95f1aa236f070715a2a6cddfd885f755e3eb8ca55cf5dd8b0b359d1a34339ac5ff933b34606e834238fe27ad07a0518575e53661350563c1d4adc476", "140849ef95f1aa236f070715a2a6cddfd885f755e3eb8ca55cf5dd8b0b359d1a34339ac5ff933b34606e834238fe27ad07a0518575e53661350563c1d4adc476"]}','2026-07-17 16:18:55.489892','2026-07-17 16:18:55.489892','aerodynamics_v1'),
	 ('682efe53-c8b5-43a3-83f7-7d9cce8be44c'::uuid,'FREE ENERGY','SYSTEM','{"{\"название\": \"FREE ENERGY\", \"описание\": \"Free energy change (ΔF), a key parameter in thermodynamics, is fundamentally linked to changes in en\"}"}','Free energy change (ΔF), a key parameter in thermodynamics, is fundamentally linked to changes in entropy and internal energy within a system. Mathematically, it can be expressed as ΔF = ΔU - T ΔS, where ΔU represents the change in internal energy and T ΔS accounts for the product of temperature (T) and change in entropy (ΔS). This expression is particularly relevant when considering systems with complex microstructures, such as those containing vacancies or exhibiting significant vibrational activity. In these contexts, additional terms related to vacancy energy and vibrational entropy are incorporated into the free energy equation, reflecting their contributions to the overall thermodynamic state of the system.','{}','{}','{"frequency": 2, "text_unit_ids": ["9b40aeeee926e9f06b82ce0583b77840ada76a848e877abeda1fe25c37d3511249a17db306eabf3940c7987d16afdb9a598d693aa693ba661c12d71e90e7f8c7", "9b40aeeee926e9f06b82ce0583b77840ada76a848e877abeda1fe25c37d3511249a17db306eabf3940c7987d16afdb9a598d693aa693ba661c12d71e90e7f8c7"]}','2026-07-17 17:14:05.801343','2026-07-17 17:14:05.801343','solid_state_physics_v1'),
	 ('01663529-6c56-449a-8011-1685d41d19c7'::uuid,'OBLIQUE SHOCK WAVE','COMPONENT','{"{\"название\": \"OBLIQUE SHOCK WAVE\", \"описание\": \"Oblique shock waves occur when flow crosses the shock front at an angle, forcing it to change direct\"}"}','Oblique shock waves occur when flow crosses the shock front at an angle, forcing it to change direction during supersonic flight around wedges or sharp conical shapes; they are characterized by a decrease in velocity','{}','{}','{"frequency": 2, "text_unit_ids": ["140849ef95f1aa236f070715a2a6cddfd885f755e3eb8ca55cf5dd8b0b359d1a34339ac5ff933b34606e834238fe27ad07a0518575e53661350563c1d4adc476", "140849ef95f1aa236f070715a2a6cddfd885f755e3eb8ca55cf5dd8b0b359d1a34339ac5ff933b34606e834238fe27ad07a0518575e53661350563c1d4adc476"]}','2026-07-17 16:18:55.489892','2026-07-17 16:18:55.489892','aerodynamics_v1'),
	 ('fca8d7c6-8d28-4d66-a708-f9f8ce0414de'::uuid,'SHOCKWAVE','MECHANISM','{"{\"название\": \"SHOCKWAVE\", \"описание\": \"An \\\"attached bow wave\\\" or \\\"oblique shock\\\" formed due to changes in the supersonic flow, with intensi\"}"}','An "attached bow wave" or "oblique shock" formed due to changes in the supersonic flow, with intensity depending on the angle of the shock relative to the incoming flow direction','{}','{}','{"frequency": 2, "text_unit_ids": ["d5f7ab80d0b58c2ff15ee04bad698949f6b490c19575d13aeeed20f431368326318208bb6da02831d9150fd85e6b6f8fb3378101b21c9f4f0102909b3e3bc2a3", "d5f7ab80d0b58c2ff15ee04bad698949f6b490c19575d13aeeed20f431368326318208bb6da02831d9150fd85e6b6f8fb3378101b21c9f4f0102909b3e3bc2a3"]}','2026-07-17 16:18:55.489892','2026-07-17 16:18:55.489892','aerodynamics_v1'),
	 ('09c8bc09-954c-4595-8a22-7853075ef5bd'::uuid,'OBLIQUE SHOCK','SYSTEM','{"{\"название\": \"OBLIQUE SHOCK\", \"описание\": \"Refers to a type of shock that forms at an angle to the flow direction and reduces the velocity of t\"}"}','Refers to a type of shock that forms at an angle to the flow direction and reduces the velocity of the gas more gently than a normal shock wave, where mu (μ) is the inclination angle.','{}','{}','{"frequency": 2, "text_unit_ids": ["d5f7ab80d0b58c2ff15ee04bad698949f6b490c19575d13aeeed20f431368326318208bb6da02831d9150fd85e6b6f8fb3378101b21c9f4f0102909b3e3bc2a3", "d5f7ab80d0b58c2ff15ee04bad698949f6b490c19575d13aeeed20f431368326318208bb6da02831d9150fd85e6b6f8fb3378101b21c9f4f0102909b3e3bc2a3"]}','2026-07-17 16:18:55.489892','2026-07-17 16:18:55.489892','aerodynamics_v1'),
	 ('61048749-1154-4005-b66e-fcfc3a60f9a9'::uuid,'FLOW DECELERATION','MECHANISM','{"{\"название\": \"FLOW DECELERATION\", \"описание\": \"A process in which supersonic flow slows down due to shock interaction, which can be of varying inte\"}"}','A process in which supersonic flow slows down due to shock interaction, which can be of varying intensity based on flow parameters such as the angle of incidence and speed','{}','{}','{"frequency": 2, "text_unit_ids": ["d5f7ab80d0b58c2ff15ee04bad698949f6b490c19575d13aeeed20f431368326318208bb6da02831d9150fd85e6b6f8fb3378101b21c9f4f0102909b3e3bc2a3", "d5f7ab80d0b58c2ff15ee04bad698949f6b490c19575d13aeeed20f431368326318208bb6da02831d9150fd85e6b6f8fb3378101b21c9f4f0102909b3e3bc2a3"]}','2026-07-17 16:18:55.489892','2026-07-17 16:18:55.489892','aerodynamics_v1');
