	 ('01a220df-c1d8-46fe-811d-cbc9535c3027'::uuid,'ΔF = −(4/3)Π R³ Λ (T_M − T)/T_M + 4Π R² Γ','MODEL','{"{\"название\": \"ΔF = −(4/3)Π R³ Λ (T_M − T)/T_M + 4Π R² Γ\", \"описание\": \"General equation describing total free energy change due to both volume and surface effects during p\"}"}','General equation describing total free energy change due to both volume and surface effects during phase transition','{}','{}','{"frequency": 3, "text_unit_ids": ["d2032ae9dddd98b060a009a328f21502528c28113460e17f3cb1218b3536aefa712a61e6b8149a0979cd51a8b20c63a51e821e71df8f19c34d6f0a736a46dac6", "d2032ae9dddd98b060a009a328f21502528c28113460e17f3cb1218b3536aefa712a61e6b8149a0979cd51a8b20c63a51e821e71df8f19c34d6f0a736a46dac6", "d2032ae9dddd98b060a009a328f21502528c28113460e17f3cb1218b3536aefa712a61e6b8149a0979cd51a8b20c63a51e821e71df8f19c34d6f0a736a46dac6"]}','2026-07-17 17:14:05.801343','2026-07-17 17:14:05.801343','solid_state_physics_v1'),
	 ('65c61ad2-1ad7-4a76-9b61-4b16a716fb85'::uuid,'CONICAL TOP','PART','{"{\"название\": \"CONICAL TOP\", \"описание\": \"Part of the design of the rocket built by Lagari Hasan Çelebi\"}"}','Part of the design of the rocket built by Lagari Hasan Çelebi','{}','{}','{"frequency": 1, "text_unit_ids": ["46b667214423448900a64449a21a8d78137e40dbbcde1ff7361b13892626a596937541e8a1dff8c28756c1af322bcfde1298239045005d93a04cd46043247c20"]}','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','history_development_aeronautics'),
	 ('aefce5fd-b673-4e42-bcee-567368880058'::uuid,'CAYLEY''S GLIDER','DEVICE','{"{\"название\": \"CAYLEY''S GLIDER\", \"описание\": \"CAYLEY''S GLIDER, developed by George Cayley in 1852, is a significant early design in aviation hist\"}"}','CAYLEY''S GLIDER, developed by George Cayley in 1852, is a significant early design in aviation history. This man-carrying glider played a pivotal role in advancing aerodynamic principles and pioneering the separation of lift, equilibrium, and propulsion tasks essential for flight. By focusing on these distinct functions, Cayley''s creation laid the groundwork for later developments in heavier-than-air machines that utilized dynamic lift mechanisms. The 1852 model marked a crucial step forward in the quest to achieve sustainable, pilot-carrying gliders, influencing subsequent generations of aerospace innovators and aircraft designs.','{}','{}','{"frequency": 3, "text_unit_ids": ["4089000a7a5f43c1f79ebd955ed69dab8fc13c6f0153fe4c6ae9df3fdfa0ecdfc28e259193c210fc04e64e6f124fe76ccb1f7ccbb3e5ccb8e8d848fbdfd2ef5c", "4089000a7a5f43c1f79ebd955ed69dab8fc13c6f0153fe4c6ae9df3fdfa0ecdfc28e259193c210fc04e64e6f124fe76ccb1f7ccbb3e5ccb8e8d848fbdfd2ef5c", "4089000a7a5f43c1f79ebd955ed69dab8fc13c6f0153fe4c6ae9df3fdfa0ecdfc28e259193c210fc04e64e6f124fe76ccb1f7ccbb3e5ccb8e8d848fbdfd2ef5c"]}','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','history_development_aeronautics'),
	 ('8ca0ec61-d72d-4025-b69f-f9e9e2bd3765'::uuid,'COMPRESSED AIR ENGINE','DEVICE','{"{\"название\": \"COMPRESSED AIR ENGINE\", \"описание\": \"\\\"COMPRESSED AIR ENGINE\\\" is an experimental engine concept proposed by Sir George Cayley in the mid-1\"}"}','"COMPRESSED AIR ENGINE" is an experimental engine concept proposed by Sir George Cayley in the mid-19th century as a potential means of aircraft propulsion. Although interesting theoretically, this design did not achieve practical success primarily due to its inherent limitations in power output and reliability. This concept represented one of several early attempts by Cayley to explore novel methods for powered flight, yet it never realized its full potential as a viable technology in aviation history.','{}','{}','{"frequency": 3, "text_unit_ids": ["4089000a7a5f43c1f79ebd955ed69dab8fc13c6f0153fe4c6ae9df3fdfa0ecdfc28e259193c210fc04e64e6f124fe76ccb1f7ccbb3e5ccb8e8d848fbdfd2ef5c", "4089000a7a5f43c1f79ebd955ed69dab8fc13c6f0153fe4c6ae9df3fdfa0ecdfc28e259193c210fc04e64e6f124fe76ccb1f7ccbb3e5ccb8e8d848fbdfd2ef5c", "4089000a7a5f43c1f79ebd955ed69dab8fc13c6f0153fe4c6ae9df3fdfa0ecdfc28e259193c210fc04e64e6f124fe76ccb1f7ccbb3e5ccb8e8d848fbdfd2ef5c"]}','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','history_development_aeronautics'),
	 ('c99f57ab-ca57-4599-9e07-6bd58ab7bcc1'::uuid,'MONTGOMERY''S GLIDER','DEVICE','{"{\"название\": \"MONTGOMERY''S GLIDER\", \"описание\": \"MONTGOMERY''S GLIDER, developed in 1884, is documented as one of the pioneering attempts in aviation\"}"}','MONTGOMERY''S GLIDER, developed in 1884, is documented as one of the pioneering attempts in aviation history. Built by an individual named Montgomery in the United States, this manned monoplane glider featured cambered aerofoils—curved surfaces that were crucial for producing lift and enhancing stability during flight. The design represented a significant early effort to achieve controlled flight capabilities, marking an important step towards the realization of heavier-than-air flight technologies.','{}','{}','{"frequency": 3, "text_unit_ids": ["4089000a7a5f43c1f79ebd955ed69dab8fc13c6f0153fe4c6ae9df3fdfa0ecdfc28e259193c210fc04e64e6f124fe76ccb1f7ccbb3e5ccb8e8d848fbdfd2ef5c", "4089000a7a5f43c1f79ebd955ed69dab8fc13c6f0153fe4c6ae9df3fdfa0ecdfc28e259193c210fc04e64e6f124fe76ccb1f7ccbb3e5ccb8e8d848fbdfd2ef5c", "4089000a7a5f43c1f79ebd955ed69dab8fc13c6f0153fe4c6ae9df3fdfa0ecdfc28e259193c210fc04e64e6f124fe76ccb1f7ccbb3e5ccb8e8d848fbdfd2ef5c"]}','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','history_development_aeronautics'),
	 ('dc5bb227-d17f-4c98-84c9-78ea16a88de6'::uuid,'OTTO LILIENTHAL''S EXPERIMENTS','MODEL','{"{\"название\": \"OTTO LILIENTHAL''S EXPERIMENTS\", \"описание\": \"OTTO LILIENTHAL''S EXPERIMENTS (1891) encompassed a series of controlled gliding experiments that in\"}"}','OTTO LILIENTHAL''S EXPERIMENTS (1891) encompassed a series of controlled gliding experiments that involved both monoplanes and biplanes. These experiments utilized wings designed with characteristics reminiscent of birds or bats, reflecting Lilienthal''s innovative approach to flight. During this period, Lilienthal employed a technique known as the whirling arm to test wing forces in free air environments. Through these experiments, he meticulously researched the principles behind flapping flight. Despite the potential shown by such designs, Lilienthal eventually abandoned the concept due to inherent limitations in achieving effective and sustainable flight through flapping mechanisms alone.
INSERT INTO agi_evolution.knowledge_nodes (id,"name",node_type,properties,description,embedding,parameters,metadata,created_at,updated_at,theme_id) VALUES
	 ('12b841cd-c596-4e14-ab64-49ad8dadde78'::uuid,'JULIEN','PERSON','{"{\"название\": \"JULIEN\", \"описание\": \"Julien''s work in 1848 involved measuring the drag of streamlined bodies using water tests.\"}"}','"Julien''s work in 1848 involved measuring the drag of streamlined bodies using water tests."','{}','{}','{"frequency": 2, "text_unit_ids": ["573d5db6e587374521f111a47eaa08e2ce573235b08716d91bbe053504fe503530293339ede873a3ac356c3d376fcb97e005ef76112125385fa9e127d8e42fec", "573d5db6e587374521f111a47eaa08e2ce573235b08716d91bbe053504fe503530293339ede873a3ac356c3d376fcb97e005ef76112125385fa9e127d8e42fec"]}','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','history_development_aeronautics'),
	 ('2741f8b7-7a0d-4d62-b5ff-ab76e455d1d3'::uuid,'SOREAU & CANOVETTI','GROUP','{"{\"название\": \"SOREAU & CANOVETTI\", \"описание\": \"Soreau and Canovetti''s pioneering research, conducted in 1903, significantly advanced the understan\"}"}','Soreau and Canovetti''s pioneering research, conducted in 1903, significantly advanced the understanding of air resistance or "drag." By conducting meticulous experiments on streamlined bodies, they were able to build upon existing knowledge in aerodynamics. The pair demonstrated a thorough approach by potentially testing these forms not only through rigorous experimental methods but also under natural wind conditions. These dual methodologies ensured a more comprehensive analysis of the forces at play, contributing valuable insights into the behaviors and characteristics of streamlined shapes as they interact with air flow.','{}','{}','{"frequency": 2, "text_unit_ids": ["573d5db6e587374521f111a47eaa08e2ce573235b08716d91bbe053504fe503530293339ede873a3ac356c3d376fcb97e005ef76112125385fa9e127d8e42fec", "573d5db6e587374521f111a47eaa08e2ce573235b08716d91bbe053504fe503530293339ede873a3ac356c3d376fcb97e005ef76112125385fa9e127d8e42fec"]}','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','history_development_aeronautics'),
	 ('740f6626-c35b-43c9-a29f-c224a7e77f68'::uuid,'STANTON','PERSON','{"{\"название\": \"STANTON\", \"описание\": \"STANTON''s tests conducted at the National Physical Laboratory (NPL) in 1904 utilized natural wind f\"}"}','STANTON''s tests conducted at the National Physical Laboratory (NPL) in 1904 utilized natural wind forces over high towers. These experiments demonstrated significant progress towards more accurate outdoor testing methods that can be applied to practical settings such as aircraft design and evaluation. This work laid foundational groundwork for advancements in aerodynamic testing and design, reflecting Stanton''s pivotal role in enhancing the reliability and applicability of outdoor test methodologies during this period.','{}','{}','{"frequency": 2, "text_unit_ids": ["573d5db6e587374521f111a47eaa08e2ce573235b08716d91bbe053504fe503530293339ede873a3ac356c3d376fcb97e005ef76112125385fa9e127d8e42fec", "573d5db6e587374521f111a47eaa08e2ce573235b08716d91bbe053504fe503530293339ede873a3ac356c3d376fcb97e005ef76112125385fa9e127d8e42fec"]}','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','history_development_aeronautics'),
	 ('e323fe4a-cb3f-48a1-b11a-da139d28a517'::uuid,'LAGARIE HASAN ÇELEBI','PERSON','{"{\"название\": \"LAGARIE HASAN ÇELEBI\", \"описание\": \"The person who conducted the first known example of a manned rocket flight during Sultan Murad IV''s\"}"}','The person who conducted the first known example of a manned rocket flight during Sultan Murad IV''s celebrations','{}','{}','{"frequency": 1, "text_unit_ids": ["624b0f2e5156161ffdb09c558f32b39ad0bf347e1dcc51d0cc803eb1592f75125b51005c9a82dfcfa9afb96df74b8311d90272937604af08308a19e41b14f3c5"]}','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','history_development_aeronautics'),
	 ('891ad321-bca9-42fe-a350-9e9790910cc7'::uuid,'LIGHTER-THAN-AIR APPARATUS','DEVICE','{"{\"название\": \"LIGHTER-THAN-AIR APPARATUS\", \"описание\": \"A flying device designed by Francesco de Lana-Terzi using spheres from which air could be evacuated \"}"}','A flying device designed by Francesco de Lana-Terzi using spheres from which air could be evacuated to decrease its density and allow it to ascend.>','{}','{}','{"frequency": 3, "text_unit_ids": ["624b0f2e5156161ffdb09c558f32b39ad0bf347e1dcc51d0cc803eb1592f75125b51005c9a82dfcfa9afb96df74b8311d90272937604af08308a19e41b14f3c5", "624b0f2e5156161ffdb09c558f32b39ad0bf347e1dcc51d0cc803eb1592f75125b51005c9a82dfcfa9afb96df74b8311d90272937604af08308a19e41b14f3c5", "624b0f2e5156161ffdb09c558f32b39ad0bf347e1dcc51d0cc803eb1592f75125b51005c9a82dfcfa9afb96df74b8311d90272937604af08308a19e41b14f3c5"]}','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','history_development_aeronautics'),
	 ('25a06cc8-90fe-4f4b-b47d-8865cc5a9552'::uuid,'ORNITHOPTER','DEVICE','{"{\"название\": \"ORNITHOPTER\", \"описание\": \"Devices designed by Leonardo da Vinci meant to mimic bird wings under human muscular power, none rea\"}"}','Devices designed by Leonardo da Vinci meant to mimic bird wings under human muscular power, none realized but influenced aerodynamic thought','{}','{}','{"frequency": 2, "text_unit_ids": ["a5d4719b2541caf004e1082010054faa38c7ba80d90b5f7e39636fab5592ad3861a1d6acd00ebc78dac62d343df8f5398463149ba9cee12a0171444fbc1a02ad", "a5d4719b2541caf004e1082010054faa38c7ba80d90b5f7e39636fab5592ad3861a1d6acd00ebc78dac62d343df8f5398463149ba9cee12a0171444fbc1a02ad"]}','2026-07-17 16:18:55.489892','2026-07-17 16:18:55.489892','aerodynamics_v1'),
	 ('4049c208-4a84-4259-8095-0cf38c4c07db'::uuid,'MODEL HELICOPTER','DEVICE','{"{\"название\": \"MODEL HELICOPTER\", \"описание\": \"The MODEL HELICOPTER represents an early technological milestone in the realm of aviation theory and\"}"}','The MODEL HELICOPTER represents an early technological milestone in the realm of aviation theory and application. Developed by a collaborative team including Ponton d''Amécourt, Nadar, and de Lalande, this device was instrumental not only as a practical tool but also served to test theoretical principles pivotal for achieving controlled flight. The development of the MODEL HELICOPTER aligns with its creators'' broader manifesto emphasizing the pursuit of controlled flight, indicating its significance in advancing the understanding and feasibility of human flight. These innovators leveraged their device to explore foundational concepts that would later be crucial in the evolution of aviation technology.','{}','{}','{"frequency": 3, "text_unit_ids": ["faa334cc3a5b50c3cebcf1df46beb7be9ad777690802933a651dec6cbd0da34c9fef6dd95627eca4b6a746fc7c67bc72b217d1c4e60e92895dbfef4b8412f573", "faa334cc3a5b50c3cebcf1df46beb7be9ad777690802933a651dec6cbd0da34c9fef6dd95627eca4b6a746fc7c67bc72b217d1c4e60e92895dbfef4b8412f573", "faa334cc3a5b50c3cebcf1df46beb7be9ad777690802933a651dec6cbd0da34c9fef6dd95627eca4b6a746fc7c67bc72b217d1c4e60e92895dbfef4b8412f573"]}','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','history_development_aeronautics'),
	 ('9c9c5562-1ef1-4c77-a694-fc05ce028454'::uuid,'LONG AND THIN WINGS','MECHANISM','{"{\"название\": \"LONG AND THIN WINGS\", \"описание\": \"Proposed wing design with a longer leading edge relative to weight, believed to be more effective ba\"}"}','Proposed wing design with a longer leading edge relative to weight, believed to be more effective based on Wenham''s research','{}','{}','{"frequency": 2, "text_unit_ids": ["a1689fa4557c7bd9828498b6af22e4d56a6e70b706bc03a66df0ec58854f6cb93cfb6e67be14e6cf7954609e79e3b6bd423a0ba59422819f13f132672854041e", "a1689fa4557c7bd9828498b6af22e4d56a6e70b706bc03a66df0ec58854f6cb93cfb6e67be14e6cf7954609e79e3b6bd423a0ba59422819f13f132672854041e"]}','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','history_development_aeronautics'),
	 ('7a00603d-b4dc-4e9f-986c-c2166b67ae51'::uuid,'CURVED WINGS','MECHANISM','{"{\"название\": \"CURVED WINGS\", \"описание\": \"CURVED WINGS are noted for their superior aerodynamic performance, having been validated through rig\"}"}','CURVED WINGS are noted for their superior aerodynamic performance, having been validated through rigorous testing. According to research conducted by Robert Wenham, these wings exhibit enhanced lift efficiency, achieving a notable lift-to-drag ratio of approximately 5:1 when tested at an angle of 15 degrees. The design proves particularly effective due to its optimized curvature, which has been confirmed through extensive wind tunnel experiments. This superior lifting ability makes CURVED WINGS a preferred choice in applications requiring high performance and efficiency in aerodynamic settings.','{}','{}','{"frequency": 2, "text_unit_ids": ["a1689fa4557c7bd9828498b6af22e4d56a6e70b706bc03a66df0ec58854f6cb93cfb6e67be14e6cf7954609e79e3b6bd423a0ba59422819f13f132672854041e", "a1689fa4557c7bd9828498b6af22e4d56a6e70b706bc03a66df0ec58854f6cb93cfb6e67be14e6cf7954609e79e3b6bd423a0ba59422819f13f132672854041e"]}','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','history_development_aeronautics'),
	 ('7711cada-8394-452b-a775-902721dfdb84'::uuid,'WILHEM KRESS''S HANG GLIDER','MECHANISM','{"{\"название\": \"WILHEM KRESS''S HANG GLIDER\", \"описание\": \"The WILHEM KRESS''S HANG GLIDER is an early aviation device constructed approximately in 1877. This \"}"}','The WILHEM KRESS''S HANG GLIDER is an early aviation device constructed approximately in 1877. This pioneering hang glider served dual purposes: it was primarily designed to explore the fundamental aerodynamic principles governing aircraft, providing crucial insights into the mechanics of flight. Additionally, this innovative device played a significant role in inspiring further developments in hang gliding and early aviation technology, marking an important milestone in the history of manned flight.','{}','{}','{"frequency": 2, "text_unit_ids": ["a1689fa4557c7bd9828498b6af22e4d56a6e70b706bc03a66df0ec58854f6cb93cfb6e67be14e6cf7954609e79e3b6bd423a0ba59422819f13f132672854041e", "a1689fa4557c7bd9828498b6af22e4d56a6e70b706bc03a66df0ec58854f6cb93cfb6e67be14e6cf7954609e79e3b6bd423a0ba59422819f13f132672854041e"]}','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','history_development_aeronautics');
