	 ('f309b580-ec65-4105-b61a-0f2ae2e6deb4'::uuid,'ELASTIC LIMIT Σ_У','MODEL','{"{\"название\": \"ELASTIC LIMIT Σ_У\", \"описание\": \"Elastic limit indicates the threshold stress at which residual longitudinal strain becomes minimal, \"}"}','"Elastic limit indicates the threshold stress at which residual longitudinal strain becomes minimal, typically within a range of 0.02…0.05%, marking the transition from elastic to potentially plastic deformation (Fig. 2.6)."','{}','{}','{"frequency": 1, "text_unit_ids": ["8b32ca58020b8954e30b675c9ce908081657304f06a9f556d8bd4206b77e8886584f55cedc137d75ad1fdfb5059f1147bcf8f982955b00ecb4cfb926e088a893"]}','2026-07-17 16:45:38.667334','2026-07-17 16:45:38.667334','sopromat_v1'),
	 ('40237e28-9ead-4c23-ac72-11cc9a31fdd1'::uuid,'ULTIMATE TENSILE STRENGTH Σ_В','MODEL','{"{\"название\": \"ULTIMATE TENSILE STRENGTH Σ_В\", \"описание\": \"Ultimate tensile strength is the highest stress level that a material can withstand before failing u\"}"}','"Ultimate tensile strength is the highest stress level that a material can withstand before failing under load, represented as the maximum load point on the specimen in a tension test diagram (Fig. 2.6)."','{}','{}','{"frequency": 1, "text_unit_ids": ["8b32ca58020b8954e30b675c9ce908081657304f06a9f556d8bd4206b77e8886584f55cedc137d75ad1fdfb5059f1147bcf8f982955b00ecb4cfb926e088a893"]}','2026-07-17 16:45:38.667334','2026-07-17 16:45:38.667334','sopromat_v1'),
	 ('5ac5c56e-d2e0-43c3-9dbe-ccc4bd8e6d3d'::uuid,'OL₁','SEGMENT','{"{\"название\": \"OL₁\", \"описание\": \"OL₁ represents residual deformation Δl_ост\"}"}','OL₁ represents residual deformation Δl_ост','{}','{}','{"frequency": 2, "text_unit_ids": ["5d7651a3b3696fb6035ceec93c2758d36c8e35b07b25de5ba53e7352573cd4ea709e865b3da28cbc013cfd5ad720acff00ce21a93b8d112d4e1f91ad7a9a1179", "5d7651a3b3696fb6035ceec93c2758d36c8e35b07b25de5ba53e7352573cd4ea709e865b3da28cbc013cfd5ad720acff00ce21a93b8d112d4e1f91ad7a9a1179"]}','2026-07-17 16:45:38.667334','2026-07-17 16:45:38.667334','sopromat_v1'),
	 ('484ff571-e125-4c3a-8c7a-4b13d2be80cb'::uuid,'OM₂','SEGMENT','{"{\"название\": \"OM₂\", \"описание\": \"Segment OM₂ represents total deformation before rupture Δl_р\"}"}','Segment OM₂ represents total deformation before rupture Δl_р','{}','{}','{"frequency": 2, "text_unit_ids": ["5d7651a3b3696fb6035ceec93c2758d36c8e35b07b25de5ba53e7352573cd4ea709e865b3da28cbc013cfd5ad720acff00ce21a93b8d112d4e1f91ad7a9a1179", "5d7651a3b3696fb6035ceec93c2758d36c8e35b07b25de5ba53e7352573cd4ea709e865b3da28cbc013cfd5ad720acff00ce21a93b8d112d4e1f91ad7a9a1179"]}','2026-07-17 16:45:38.667334','2026-07-17 16:45:38.667334','sopromat_v1'),
	 ('32a1e319-336d-4e86-908e-7f57333e2f66'::uuid,'OM₁','SEGMENT','{"{\"название\": \"OM₁\", \"описание\": \"Segment OM₁ measures residual deformation after failure Δl_ост\"}"}','Segment OM₁ measures residual deformation after failure Δl_ост','{}','{}','{"frequency": 2, "text_unit_ids": ["5d7651a3b3696fb6035ceec93c2758d36c8e35b07b25de5ba53e7352573cd4ea709e865b3da28cbc013cfd5ad720acff00ce21a93b8d112d4e1f91ad7a9a1179", "5d7651a3b3696fb6035ceec93c2758d36c8e35b07b25de5ba53e7352573cd4ea709e865b3da28cbc013cfd5ad720acff00ce21a93b8d112d4e1f91ad7a9a1179"]}','2026-07-17 16:45:38.667334','2026-07-17 16:45:38.667334','sopromat_v1'),
	 ('298af4b4-fbd5-40db-8bb0-6249e027f0ba'::uuid,'YIELD PLATEAU DISAPPEARS','PROPERTY','{"{\"название\": \"YIELD PLATEAU DISAPPEARS\", \"описание\": \"Strain hardening causes the yield plateau to disappear, indicating changes in material behavior\"}"}','Strain hardening causes the yield plateau to disappear, indicating changes in material behavior','{}','{}','{"frequency": 1, "text_unit_ids": ["5d7651a3b3696fb6035ceec93c2758d36c8e35b07b25de5ba53e7352573cd4ea709e865b3da28cbc013cfd5ad720acff00ce21a93b8d112d4e1f91ad7a9a1179"]}','2026-07-17 16:45:38.667334','2026-07-17 16:45:38.667334','sopromat_v1'),
	 ('7c7daa8a-d29d-46b9-8139-e36db62096f3'::uuid,'CYLINDRICAL STEEL AND CAST-IRON SPECIMENS','DEVICE','{"{\"название\": \"CYLINDRICAL STEEL AND CAST-IRON SPECIMENS\", \"описание\": \"These specimens with diameters d₀ = 6…25 mm and L₀/d₀ ratio of 1…2 are used for compression tests\"}"}','These specimens with diameters d₀ = 6…25 mm and L₀/d₀ ratio of 1…2 are used for compression tests','{}','{}','{"frequency": 1, "text_unit_ids": ["5d7651a3b3696fb6035ceec93c2758d36c8e35b07b25de5ba53e7352573cd4ea709e865b3da28cbc013cfd5ad720acff00ce21a93b8d112d4e1f91ad7a9a1179"]}','2026-07-17 16:45:38.667334','2026-07-17 16:45:38.667334','sopromat_v1'),
	 ('9b79ef33-16a4-40aa-b419-d886a0e2b752'::uuid,'IRON SPECIMENS','MATERIAL','{"{\"название\": \"IRON SPECIMENS\", \"описание\": \"Iron specimens with a diameter range of 6…25 mm are used in the experiments. The length to diameter \"}"}','Iron specimens with a diameter range of 6…25 mm are used in the experiments. The length to diameter ratio L₀/d₀ varies from 1 to 2.','{}','{}','{"frequency": 1, "text_unit_ids": ["505daa15cbea14b13f2f7492eb480c452a365dc8a047f6c2292e974d156c07a2c5b349dee0fe6cfd6455953f8f53913648f5bcf35c450aa7516e5fb440c2377f"]}','2026-07-17 16:45:38.667334','2026-07-17 16:45:38.667334','sopromat_v1'),
	 ('b9cb6644-4de4-4ce4-8d32-ad4a08cae595'::uuid,'STEEL SPECIMEN','MATERIAL','{"{\"название\": \"STEEL SPECIMEN\", \"описание\": \"Steel specimen which is used for tension and compression tests, its stress-strain diagram shows a li\"}"}','Steel specimen which is used for tension and compression tests, its stress-strain diagram shows a linear portion initially, then bends at the yield point where the strength properties are calculated based on forces F_п and F_т. The ultimate compressive strength of steel equals its tensile strength if no distinct yield plateau can be observed.','{}','{}','{"frequency": 2, "text_unit_ids": ["505daa15cbea14b13f2f7492eb480c452a365dc8a047f6c2292e974d156c07a2c5b349dee0fe6cfd6455953f8f53913648f5bcf35c450aa7516e5fb440c2377f", "505daa15cbea14b13f2f7492eb480c452a365dc8a047f6c2292e974d156c07a2c5b349dee0fe6cfd6455953f8f53913648f5bcf35c450aa7516e5fb440c2377f"]}','2026-07-17 16:45:38.667334','2026-07-17 16:45:38.667334','sopromat_v1'),
	 ('82e14225-4ade-40d0-99a3-5d6e8d1394a2'::uuid,'LIMIT STATE METHOD','MODEL','{"{\"название\": \"LIMIT STATE METHOD\", \"описание\": \"(An advanced safety assessment methodology) This approach defines failure as reaching a specific saf\"}"}','(An advanced safety assessment methodology) This approach defines failure as reaching a specific safety limit state wherein the system ceases to perform its intended function; it is crucial for ensuring the safety and reliability of structures subjected to various types of loads over different time periods. The limit states could be ultimate (maximum load capacity), serviceability (minimum acceptable performance level during usage), or both.','{}','{}','{"frequency": 2, "text_unit_ids": ["505daa15cbea14b13f2f7492eb480c452a365dc8a047f6c2292e974d156c07a2c5b349dee0fe6cfd6455953f8f53913648f5bcf35c450aa7516e5fb440c2377f", "505daa15cbea14b13f2f7492eb480c452a365dc8a047f6c2292e974d156c07a2c5b349dee0fe6cfd6455953f8f53913648f5bcf35c450aa7516e5fb440c2377f"]}','2026-07-17 16:45:38.667334','2026-07-17 16:45:38.667334','sopromat_v1');
INSERT INTO agi_evolution.knowledge_nodes (id,"name",node_type,properties,description,embedding,parameters,metadata,created_at,updated_at,theme_id) VALUES
	 ('b29f49cc-06b9-44b7-a562-65426f7a9654'::uuid,'SAFETY FACTOR N','MODEL','{"{\"название\": \"SAFETY FACTOR N\", \"описание\": \"SAFETY FACTOR N is a critical component in allowable stress methods used to ensure the safe operatio\"}"}','SAFETY FACTOR N is a critical component in allowable stress methods used to ensure the safe operation of structures under various load conditions. This coefficient accounts for variability and uncertainty factors such as material imperfections, environmental conditions, among others, guaranteeing that structures can withstand not only expected loads but also unexpected ones exceeding their calculated yield strength or ultimate capacity. By incorporating these variability and uncertainty factors, SAFETY FACTOR N plays a pivotal role in enhancing the reliability and safety of structural designs.','{}','{}','{"frequency": 2, "text_unit_ids": ["505daa15cbea14b13f2f7492eb480c452a365dc8a047f6c2292e974d156c07a2c5b349dee0fe6cfd6455953f8f53913648f5bcf35c450aa7516e5fb440c2377f", "505daa15cbea14b13f2f7492eb480c452a365dc8a047f6c2292e974d156c07a2c5b349dee0fe6cfd6455953f8f53913648f5bcf35c450aa7516e5fb440c2377f"]}','2026-07-17 16:45:38.667334','2026-07-17 16:45:38.667334','sopromat_v1'),
	 ('426e9daa-1e85-4383-a4f2-cfde3b4d475f'::uuid,'PRINCIPAL STRESSES','MECHANISM','{"{\"название\": \"PRINCIPAL STRESSES\", \"описание\": \"Principal stresses are calculated by averaging principal stresses and adding or subtracting half of \"}"}','Principal stresses are calculated by averaging principal stresses and adding or subtracting half of the square root term, and they act on planes inclined at 45° to the principal planes','{}','{}','{"frequency": 1, "text_unit_ids": ["ba4a007bb365126aa7e8e33dc56899336b43dcbbadb346956c52c0a58b0c709f36261ef69bd522c34f568acb3261563a7cc0f462aa9f987b85cee763f3d4ee40"]}','2026-07-17 16:45:38.667334','2026-07-17 16:45:38.667334','sopromat_v1'),
	 ('8676f68b-534e-45fc-94c0-56b03512059c'::uuid,'SHEAR STRESS','MECHANISM','{"{\"название\": \"SHEAR STRESS\", \"описание\": \"SHEAR STRESS is a type of mechanical stress that occurs when parallel forces act tangentially along \"}"}','SHEAR STRESS is a type of mechanical stress that occurs when parallel forces act tangentially along adjacent surfaces of contacting elements of a material. It is characterized by its action on mutually perpendicular planes and is mathematically related to the shear modulus (G) through Hooke''s law, expressed as τ = G γ, where γ represents the shear angle between affected elements. This relationship indicates that the magnitude of shear stress (τ) is directly proportional to the shear modulus (G) and the shear angle (γ), establishing a fundamental connection in material mechanics for understanding deformation under tangential forces.','{}','{}','{"frequency": 2, "text_unit_ids": ["ba4a007bb365126aa7e8e33dc56899336b43dcbbadb346956c52c0a58b0c709f36261ef69bd522c34f568acb3261563a7cc0f462aa9f987b85cee763f3d4ee40", "ba4a007bb365126aa7e8e33dc56899336b43dcbbadb346956c52c0a58b0c709f36261ef69bd522c34f568acb3261563a7cc0f462aa9f987b85cee763f3d4ee40"]}','2026-07-17 16:45:38.667334','2026-07-17 16:45:38.667334','sopromat_v1'),
	 ('7ba4f7d7-7440-4312-9c55-fc97d4786a11'::uuid,'NORMAL STRESSES','PRINCIPAL STRESSES','{"{\"название\": \"NORMAL STRESSES\", \"описание\": \"Normal stresses are the principal stresses within a material, ordered such that \\\\( \\\\sigma_1 \\\\geq \\\\si\"}"}','Normal stresses are the principal stresses within a material, ordered such that \( \sigma_1 \geq \sigma_2 \geq \sigma_3 \)','{}','{}','{"frequency": 1, "text_unit_ids": ["f1924e428147d032214a827807ef8f3ae81a4a9a21a9475005384b86a1f6a254489f6244b8458ae3e7a32a74c614e716d0e2e0063444283f4bb51a4c47f265a0"]}','2026-07-17 16:45:38.667334','2026-07-17 16:45:38.667334','sopromat_v1'),
	 ('bb806af5-f8ea-4361-b05d-768a5d4797c8'::uuid,'GAUZES','MECHANISM','{"{\"название\": \"GAUZES\", \"описание\": \"GAUZES, components utilized in wind tunnel design, play a crucial role in enhancing flow quality and\"}"}','GAUZES, components utilized in wind tunnel design, play a crucial role in enhancing flow quality and reducing turbulence levels. These gauzes were developed through advancements led by Gustave Eiffel, who incorporated them to improve the testing environment in his wind tunnels. Later, further refinements and experimental improvements contributed by L. Prandtl and other researchers built upon these initial developments, ensuring that gauges continued to serve as effective tools for achieving better flow quality in advanced wind tunnel systems. Through collaborative efforts and iterative improvements, GAUZES have become essential elements in the continuous refinement of aerodynamic testing methodologies.','{}','{}','{"frequency": 2, "text_unit_ids": ["6c043286a724707e324c0aa9bd1e28f9c44eaaaa396eebf578400d5cb0cb167ac12bec61fdd45d7cfa6f63f53e15f92c08aeae6493271704143d122caa10dcec", "6c043286a724707e324c0aa9bd1e28f9c44eaaaa396eebf578400d5cb0cb167ac12bec61fdd45d7cfa6f63f53e15f92c08aeae6493271704143d122caa10dcec"]}','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','history_development_aeronautics'),
	 ('af7b60f0-97b2-4627-b500-e211d4f7c28c'::uuid,'ZHUKOVSKY TUNNEL','SYSTEM','{"{\"название\": \"ZHUKOVSKY TUNNEL\", \"описание\": \"The Zhukovsky Tunnel, closely associated with the pioneering work of Nikolai Zhukovsky at Moscow Uni\"}"}','The Zhukovsky Tunnel, closely associated with the pioneering work of Nikolai Zhukovsky at Moscow University in Russia around 1902, refers to a wind tunnel that was constructed by Zhukovsky. The tunnel featured a straight square section design with windows, designed for aerodynamic research and experimentation. Although specific details about its exact specifications were not fully detailed in the available information, it is clear that this significant engineering project was completed during the same year or very close to 1902. This structure played an important role in advancing aviation technology and theoretical aeronautical science within the institution, marking a crucial milestone in early aerodynamics studies by Zhukovsky and his contemporaries.','{}','{}','{"frequency": 2, "text_unit_ids": ["af0b7dc953d20f99423204bc6976714fb8bc794b04cf5ce8101cfceef20985a957bc6eca2691ec075aaa01420b302e2b2b0c8d5a5c0d508a6dabb65c91d84d5a", "f2ee2a48ece9792c2a41e9ef8523bac39c978616667ba97f16a7e58a5f9587b6b64e5046d7ff5d1443f11029123fc3893dc0c15cfc70ec93778bbea10e47f9f7"]}','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','history_development_aeronautics'),
	 ('bd2bb085-db2b-419c-a5f0-eb546fbaf925'::uuid,'EIFFEL TUNNEL AT CHAMP DES MARS','DEVICE','{"{\"название\": \"EIFFEL TUNNEL AT CHAMP DES MARS\", \"описание\": \"The EIFFEL TUNNEL AT CHAMP DES MARS is a significant engineering structure that has served as a vita\"}"}','The EIFFEL TUNNEL AT CHAMP DES MARS is a significant engineering structure that has served as a vital facility for aerodynamic testing for over five decades. This large wind tunnel, featuring a 1.5 m diameter and an open jet design with a sealed room, was initially established by the renowned engineer Gustave Eiffel in 1909. The tunnel continued to be in active use until approximately 1960, signifying its enduring reliability and relevance in the field of aerodynamics throughout that period. This equipment played a crucial role in advancing our understanding of air flow dynamics and contributed to various technological developments during its operational lifespan.','{}','{}','{"frequency": 2, "text_unit_ids": ["6c043286a724707e324c0aa9bd1e28f9c44eaaaa396eebf578400d5cb0cb167ac12bec61fdd45d7cfa6f63f53e15f92c08aeae6493271704143d122caa10dcec", "6c043286a724707e324c0aa9bd1e28f9c44eaaaa396eebf578400d5cb0cb167ac12bec61fdd45d7cfa6f63f53e15f92c08aeae6493271704143d122caa10dcec"]}','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','2026-07-17 13:19:24.183818','history_development_aeronautics'),
	 ('67323a96-b083-473a-b7f9-9ebcf232f517'::uuid,'CR体结构中的原子、分子或离子的空间周期性排列','SYSTEM','{"{\"название\": \"CR体结构中的原子、分子或离子的空间周期性排列\", \"описание\": \"crystalline structure involves the periodic arrangement of particles such as atoms, molecules, or io\"}"}','crystalline structure involves the periodic arrangement of particles such as atoms, molecules, or ions in solids. It is determined by the spatial geometry of the crystal and its parameters.">','{}','{}','{"frequency": 1, "text_unit_ids": ["c443500ac401640e03812c68676ef2dc1b1766ba215011910bb4f476158764d339513dcb296b6be6ef5e21add844b582b4bb8f06949f4f8226ad3f8655aedb9b"]}','2026-07-17 17:14:05.801343','2026-07-17 17:14:05.801343','solid_state_physics_v1'),
	 ('dae0fa72-cfee-452a-84d7-901902ea7043'::uuid,'ATOMS, MOLECULES, IONS','COMPONENT','{"{\"название\": \"ATOMS, MOLECULES, IONS\", \"описание\": \"The entities \\\"atoms, molecules, and ions\\\" represent the fundamental building blocks that constitute \"}"}','The entities "atoms, molecules, and ions" represent the fundamental building blocks that constitute the crystalline structures found within solid materials. These units are meticulously organized in a periodic pattern, forming what is known as a crystal lattice. This arrangement significantly influences various physical properties of the material. Atoms, which can aggregate into molecules or dissociate to form ions, are the primary components responsible for creating this ordered structure. Together, they establish a regular spatial order that pervades throughout the crystalline substance, thereby dictating its macroscopic characteristics.','{}','{}','{"frequency": 2, "text_unit_ids": ["c443500ac401640e03812c68676ef2dc1b1766ba215011910bb4f476158764d339513dcb296b6be6ef5e21add844b582b4bb8f06949f4f8226ad3f8655aedb9b", "c443500ac401640e03812c68676ef2dc1b1766ba215011910bb4f476158764d339513dcb296b6be6ef5e21add844b582b4bb8f06949f4f8226ad3f8655aedb9b"]}','2026-07-17 17:14:05.801343','2026-07-17 17:14:05.801343','solid_state_physics_v1'),
	 ('d2a9fbec-d2f8-4f3d-8ac6-429bf9fe244a'::uuid,'SOLID STATE PHYSICS','SYSTEM','{"{\"название\": \"SOLID STATE PHYSICS\", \"описание\": \"SOLID STATE PHYSICS is a scientific field dedicated to investigating the physical properties of soli\"}"}','SOLID STATE PHYSICS is a scientific field dedicated to investigating the physical properties of solid materials. This discipline utilizes quantum-statistical methods to comprehend the behavior and interactions among particles that form single-crystal lattices, thereby explaining the diverse properties exhibited by crystalline solids. Solid state physics explores not only the structure and composition but also delves into understanding how these microscopic interactions influence macroscopic properties of crystals, providing a bridge between fundamental physical laws and practical applications in materials science and engineering.','{}','{}','{"frequency": 2, "text_unit_ids": ["c443500ac401640e03812c68676ef2dc1b1766ba215011910bb4f476158764d339513dcb296b6be6ef5e21add844b582b4bb8f06949f4f8226ad3f8655aedb9b", "c443500ac401640e03812c68676ef2dc1b1766ba215011910bb4f476158764d339513dcb296b6be6ef5e21add844b582b4bb8f06949f4f8226ad3f8655aedb9b"]}','2026-07-17 17:14:05.801343','2026-07-17 17:14:05.801343','solid_state_physics_v1');
INSERT INTO agi_evolution.knowledge_nodes (id,"name",node_type,properties,description,embedding,parameters,metadata,created_at,updated_at,theme_id) VALUES
	 ('223c1a8f-931a-4495-839e-d2a0b75d7e32'::uuid,'LATTICE NODE','COMPONENT','{"{\"название\": \"LATTICE NODE\", \"описание\": \"A point of intersection where translations meet to define the spatial lattice. May or may not be loc\"}"}','A point of intersection where translations meet to define the spatial lattice. May or may not be located at an atom''s center of mass>','{}','{}','{"frequency": 1, "text_unit_ids": ["be33f42641907295f83a337f4d06f95089e64774104fe7cec50db44a6a96d197ee77d4d46980237695981aeb6aed7f1827d31db11ce1ba5714986292f916aee0"]}','2026-07-17 17:14:05.801343','2026-07-17 17:14:05.801343','solid_state_physics_v1'),
	 ('f0066a8a-7842-4e19-b627-7507dcee9ec7'::uuid,'UNIT CELL','SYSTEM','{"{\"название\": \"UNIT CELL\", \"описание\": \"A unit cell is an essential geometric concept used to understand the structure of crystals. Specific\"}"}','A unit cell is an essential geometric concept used to understand the structure of crystals. Specifically, it refers to the Wigner–Seitz cell process and is defined as a specific geometric shape in three-dimensional space. This shape repeats itself when translated in all three directions by integer multiples of its dimensions, thus generating the entire crystal structure. The unit cell is characterized by three angles (α, β, and γ) and three cell parameters, which together determine the shape and volume of the unit cell. Additionally, the Bravais method plays a crucial role in defining the smallest cell, or lattice point, that completely describes the crystal structure. This smallest unit encompasses all necessary information about the crystal’s symmetry and periodicity, making it a fundamental tool for crystallography and materials science research.','{}','{}','{"frequency": 3, "text_unit_ids": ["be33f42641907295f83a337f4d06f95089e64774104fe7cec50db44a6a96d197ee77d4d46980237695981aeb6aed7f1827d31db11ce1ba5714986292f916aee0", "de853bfe49f3934f3f091e273d7f490dd0799663d94d77bcd0cf7c1bbdee2bd4306455461b629588031c9581ff98e284a6026eebc4f0f469865a92862692afbc", "091c2bdcc29b966207eedad51eb8990dd1419da9354df05045326857c5fbf87d3c068e7c25d9b5302985a77f5c66a9a1a57d7703770ab76d586d72af540195a3"]}','2026-07-17 17:14:05.801343','2026-07-17 17:14:05.801343','solid_state_physics_v1'),
	 ('fbbe0176-ed5f-4992-b8fb-2d1ca72524b8'::uuid,'CUBIC CELL','MODEL','{"{\"название\": \"CUBIC CELL\", \"описание\": \"Cubic cells represent the most symmetric structure among all crystal lattice forms, characterized by\"}"}','Cubic cells represent the most symmetric structure among all crystal lattice forms, characterized by equal cell parameters a=b=c','{}','{}','{"frequency": 1, "text_unit_ids": ["de853bfe49f3934f3f091e273d7f490dd0799663d94d77bcd0cf7c1bbdee2bd4306455461b629588031c9581ff98e284a6026eebc4f0f469865a92862692afbc"]}','2026-07-17 17:14:05.801343','2026-07-17 17:14:05.801343','solid_state_physics_v1');
